        <mxCell id="mRtqyXpgbR3qekdRVjHb-35" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Force detach&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Force detach&quot; functionality allows distributed systems to implement failover &amp;amp; failback functionality. During &quot;failover&quot; process, &quot;force detach&quot; ensures that the process will not be able to write data.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On the &quot;failback&quot;, the client will create a new instance of the bdev.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;Open isssue&lt;/font&gt;: udevd is using the bdev unique identifier to create different options to open the bdev. We don&#39;t know what will happen on failback.&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="mRtqyXpgbR3qekdRVjHb-38">
          <mxGeometry x="10" y="200" width="680" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
